.TH ROGDELTA 1 "August 2026" "rogdelta 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rogdelta \- control the ASUS ROG Delta II headset on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rogdelta
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rogdelta
provides a desktop control center, PipeWire volume and mute controls,
EasyEffects sound profiles, device status, and passive HID report capture.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B desktop
Open the desktop application window.
.TP
.B serve
Run the local web service on 127.0.0.1:17890.
.TP
.B status
Show headset connection and HID information as JSON.
.TP
.BI "volume " 0-100
Set the default PipeWire output volume.
.TP
.B mute
Toggle output mute.
.TP
.B mic-mute
Toggle microphone mute.
.TP
.BI "preset " name
Apply balanced, movie, gaming, communication, music, or bass.
.TP
.B record
Passively record HID reports. See rogdelta help for options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/99-rog-delta-ii.rules
Grants the active local user access to the supported headset HID interface.
